    <item>
      <title>Arcs</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/arcs/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/arcs/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>Alfred had known two girls during his time in London. One was a lawyer who liked to talk about her IT contract law cases. The other one was an art historian who liked to talk about which gallery would pay her to sell paintings. Alfred wanted to marry, therefore had to find a woman. He searched his conscience, and went for the one with the widest ass.
Curves weren’t just the cardinal criterion of his matrimonial quests, they were also the main ingredient of his daily cycling commute. A daily total of 43 left turns and 31 right turns, plus a mile along the winding Thames, and consider the fact that few of his London roads were perfectly straight.
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Live at the Baby Seal</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/live-at-the-baby-seal/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/live-at-the-baby-seal/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>&ldquo;Can I have a double Martini no ice, please?&rdquo;
&ldquo;We&rsquo;re actually out of Martini, I&rsquo;m very sorry. Can I offer you the house scotch instead alright?&rdquo;
&ldquo;Er..&rdquo;
&ldquo;We brew it ourselves, it&rsquo;s been aged backstage for the last couple of years, this batch just came out, alright. We get good feedback from it.&rdquo;
&ldquo;Yeah, I mean, is it the same..&rdquo;
&ldquo;&hellip;Price? Half-price this week only, alright, during weekdays.&rdquo;
&ldquo;Alright, let&rsquo;s do it.&rdquo;
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Beautiful, the Abstract, and the Absolutely Necessary</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-beautiful-the-abstract-and-the-absolutely-necessary/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-beautiful-the-abstract-and-the-absolutely-necessary/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description> Poetry does not speak, it convulses, shuddering like a wounded archangel in the throat of infinity. It is the volcanic hemorrhage of truth upon the alabaster of silence, a delirium that rends the cosmos into trembling syllables. Where language expires, Poetry thrashes – a sacred spasm, crowning the abyss with fire. Speaking of abyss, i am walking underground in a tunnel in a train station in poetic company because i&rsquo;m with my friend Jano and he&rsquo;s a poet. this may be a pedestrian tunnel but our conversation is in the stratosphere because it&rsquo;s about our appreciation of The Beautiful and the Abstract so in this tunnel we&rsquo;re two shopping carts of ontology floating down a stream of commuter spillover.
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Bench It Is</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-bench-it-is/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-bench-it-is/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>I hadn’t left Paris for too long. I mean left Paris, not just going somewhere for the weekend, in the knowledge that I had an approximate 36 hours of mitigated freedom before I need to put myself to bed eight hours before the alarm clock rings for me to be in decent lucid shape Monday morning at the office.
The office… From September 2006 to June 2009 I studied philosophy at a university that had four obligatory hours of class per week. You could decide not to go to lectures (of which you had four hours per week too). You bet I had tons of what was innocently called “independent study time“, but which was basically unconstrained free time with random bouts of studying. I had truckloads of time for myself, and in hindsight I believe I didn’t use it wisely.
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Boiled Tomato Technique</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-boiled-tomato-technique/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-boiled-tomato-technique/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>
The Boiled Tomato Technique will not only boost your dating productivity, it will give you a life-long skill to help you achieve goals. Based on more than two weeks of refinement and thinking, it’s easy to understand and highly enjoyable.
You go on a first date, by the third second your genitals establish that the person isn&rsquo;t physically attractive, by the third minute your brain yawns that they aren’t mentally attractive either. But! You&rsquo;ve sunk something like 5-10 days of your time texting frivolities with this person; your time investment hitherto is exponentially higher than three minutes. Bailing out of the date means losing that investment.
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Chatty Chakras</title>
