    <item>
      <title>The Flavour of Facts</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-flavour-of-facts/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-flavour-of-facts/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>
Guy goes to an ice cream shop, walks up, peculiarly goes:
&ldquo;Do you have cucumber ice cream please&rdquo;
&ldquo;Nn-what? Cucum&hellip; We don&rsquo;t.. We don&rsquo;t have cucumber ice cream here&rdquo;
&ldquo;Ah ok thanks&rdquo;
Walks out.
Next day, same guy goes to the ice cream shop, big line, he stands in line for 20 minutes, finally gets to the counter, and orders:
&ldquo;Do you have cucumber ice cream please&rdquo;
&ldquo;Hi there. We don&rsquo;t have cucumber ice cream, sorry&rdquo;
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>How Everything Is</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/how-everything-is/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/how-everything-is/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>Hey
How is everything
[ 3 weeks later ]
at first i was humbled and inspired by this opportunity to explore the vastness of the cosmos
contemplate the intricacies of its deepest secrets
but this task&hellip; its sheer magnitude quickly became daunting. you wanted me to inspect every molecule in the universe? this felt delusional
but i remained hopeful and duty-bound to you my dear friend
On the afternoon of the 4th day i finished accounting for the larger molecules within my apartment. i observed and analysed the behavior of the carbon-based solids i could find, as well as the production of various other gases in the premises
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>My Career with the Pope and Horses and CEOs</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/my-career-with-the-pope-and-horses-and-ceos/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/my-career-with-the-pope-and-horses-and-ceos/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>Franco says I need to focus, so today I&rsquo;ll start this journal to think of new projects I can focus on, dedicate my life to.
I&rsquo;ve ruled out starting a contemporary art museum, because I&rsquo;d have to throw away all the artwork after ten years.
I could bet on horses instead.
What if I don&rsquo;t win?
Well I&rsquo;ll get to wear obnoxious clothes at the races.
I mean at least I&rsquo;ll try. And just who doesn&rsquo;t love a ridiculous hat?!??
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Old Man And The Feelings</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-old-man-and-the-feelings/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-old-man-and-the-feelings/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>He was an old man who fished alone in a skiff on the Gulf Stream, and he had gone eighty-four days now without hurting anyone’s feelings. The fish had grown used to him, and he to them, in the way that rivals come to understand one another, except the old man did not see them as rivals. He saw them as souls.
The water was calm, the sun high. He let his line out gently, careful not to startle the fish below. In his youth, he would have cast with hubris. Now, he cast with emotional availability.
</description>
    </item>
