    <item>
      <title>Peanuts</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/peanuts/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/peanuts/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>I was walking down the street eating peanuts out of a bag of peanuts and tossing the shells on the ground until street justice warrior intervenes, says &ldquo;don&rsquo;t throw the fucking shells on the ground&rdquo;
&ldquo;they&rsquo;re biodegradable.&rdquo;
&ldquo;your mother is biodegradable&rdquo;
Mom is biodegradable, as a matter of fact. As a putrid matter of fact. Checkmate. I flick my king:
&ldquo;ok boss&rdquo;
I call strangers &ldquo;boss&rdquo; in a sanitised handful of rare cases. One of these cases is when they assert spontaneous intellectual superiority. I&rsquo;m probably in the presence of an international grandmaster. I need to do what&rsquo;s best for my family before it gets ugly.
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Pedaler of Enlightenment</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-pedaler-of-enlightenment/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-pedaler-of-enlightenment/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>A runway extends towards the vanishing point, punctuated by a few dog walkers, the sporadic kite flyer, and a cyclist charging furiously down the tarmac, sitting erect, hands grasping his lap in quiet determination. We stand witness to the charm of Berlin&rsquo;s retired Tempelhof Airport, founded in 1936, exuding the revolting charm of despotism and ideological divide, now thriving as a public park favoured by the aforementioned tethered promenaders, wind jockeys, and aspirants to the World Record for Longest Distance Cycled Without Holding The Handlebars.
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Reliable Massage</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/reliable-massage/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/reliable-massage/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>“Ok welcome, welcome. So this, this is the Fedfer Writers Workshop. You are most of you are regulars, but just for the few newcomers, what we like to do is we like to read the piece together. And&hellip; Twice if it&rsquo;s a poem, once if it&rsquo;s prose. And then we have to discuss, give feedback both to the author and to the group in general, and have discussion: what do you think works, what do you think works less. We can also discuss&hellip; Excuse me no side discussion, please. We have to discuss the piece in the context, where is it in the book also, so yeah, if you bring a chapter from the middle of a book and then you should also introduce the characters, and, I mean, yeah unless those characters have been presented here before, so&hellip; OK, and please keep your comments short, possibly on the minute, cause, again, we are many and we try to bring as many people in the conversation as we can. Alright, so&hellip; Martina is first. Who wants to read this? Are you feeling like reading Martina&rsquo;s story&hellip; Ed?”
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>El Sabor De Los Hechos</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/el-sabor-de-los-hechos/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/el-sabor-de-los-hechos/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>
Un tipo va a una heladería, se acerca, peculiarmente dice:
&ldquo;¿Tiene helado de pepino, por favor?&rdquo;
&ldquo;¿Nn-qué? Pepino&hellip; No tenemos&hellip; No tenemos helado de pepino aquí&rdquo;
&ldquo;Ah ok gracias&rdquo;
Se va.
Al día siguiente, el mismo tipo aparece en la heladería, hay una cola enorme, hace cola durante 32 minutos, por fin llega al mostrador y pide:
&ldquo;¿Tiene helado de pepino, por favor?&rdquo;
&ldquo;Hola. No, no tenemos helado de pepino, lo siento&rdquo;.
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>La Tecnica del Pomodoro Bollito™</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/la-tecnica-del-pomodoro-bollito/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/la-tecnica-del-pomodoro-bollito/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>
La Tecnica del Pomodoro Bollito™ aumenterà la vostra produttività negli appuntamenti galanti e vi garantirà l&rsquo;acquisizione di una competenza duratura per il perseguimento di qualunque finalità. Essa rappresenta il frutto di oltre due settimane di accurata elaborazione e ponderazione critica, risultando di facile comprensione e sorprendentemente piacevole da mettere in pratica.
Andate a un primo appuntamento, al terzo secondo i vostri genitali stabiliscono che la persona non è fisicamente attraente, al terzo minuto il vostro cervello sbadiglia constatando che non lo è neppure mentalmente. Ma! Avete investito una decina di giorni scambiando frivolezze con questa persona; un sostanziale investimento, ritirarsi dall&rsquo;appuntamento significa perderlo.
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The Happiest Person Alive</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-happiest-person-alive/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/the-happiest-person-alive/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>My plane is in the middle of the air when a commotion belches out a few rows ahead, people shrieking, clapping, extend my neck to see what&rsquo;s happening. There&rsquo;s this dude kneeling in the aisle with a small box clutched in his palm. Guy&rsquo;s doing a marriage proposal way above the ground.
In front of this guy is his woman, standing in the aisle, her hands classically over her mouth, her eyes jumping around the cabin.
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>A Tractate on the Cultivation of What Can&#39;t Be Harvested</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/a-tractate-on-the-cultivation-of-what-cant-be-harvested/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/a-tractate-on-the-cultivation-of-what-cant-be-harvested/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>It&rsquo;s been one month since I harrowed my relationship with my former girlfriend after I told her that I had gone for a walk in an orange grove near our house, peaceful and green, until i saw a kid sitting on a large rock, crying miserably
&ldquo;qué pasa, niño?&rdquo; i asked, crouching beside him
&ldquo;my tia Consuelo died&rdquo;, he said, and i asked him &ldquo;was she ill&rdquo; and he said no, &ldquo;the tractor. she died under the tractor&rdquo;, and i said that im sorry what a terrible accident, the government must take measures to reduce worplace accidents and ensure the safety of us all
</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Trail Mix</title>
      <link>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/trail-mix/</link>
      <guid>https://narravaganza.lol/stories/trail-mix/</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <description>The hikers stop meandering and rest in a secluded cove. Oblivious to the doom that stalks their steps. As of right now, they&rsquo;re four hours into the wilderness; isolation wraps around them like a shroud, muffling possible shrieks and screams. They now eat in silence, but this fragile peace breaks when a girl named Raisinée joins the eatery by unveiling a bag containing grapes that had been stabbed on a skewer.
</description>
    </item>
